      "content": "That's a decent start but it's a bit surface level for a grad paper. Can you go deeper into the actual philosophical/theological reasoning? Like, i'm looking for the nuance. I want to see how the liberal side constructs their argument around things like compassion or personhood, and how the conservative side builds their case beyond just saying 'it's God's will.' Can you give me a more detailed breakdown of the logical structures used by both?",
